      "description": "Watch Cercle Brugge vs St. Truiden highlights and goals from Jupiler Pro League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 17, 2026. The Jupiler Pro League clash between Cercle Brugge and Lommel United delivered a high-scoring spectacle defined by shifting momentums. Both sides contributed to a relentless attacking display that left the result hanging in the balance until the final moments. Lommel's First-Half Blitz On August 17, 2026 , the game exploded into life from the very first whistle. Within sixty seconds, Ryan Merlen put Lommel United ahead, converting a pass from Ilias Sebaoui . The visitors remained clinical throughout the opening period, exploiting gaps in the home defense. In the 28th minute, Steve Ngoura doubled the lead, showcasing the tactical discipline of the visiting side. Lommel's dominance was further underlined before the break. In the 37th minute, Ryan Merlen struck again to secure his brace, following an assist from Robert-Jan Vanwesemael . Heading into the interval with a significant advantage, the visitors appeared to be in total control of the narrative at the Jan Breydel Stadium . Second Half Drama and Fightback The restart saw Nelson Ishiwatari extend the lead in the 47th minute, once again set up by Ilias Sebaoui . However, the introduction of fresh legs sparked a late surge from Cercle Brugge . Erick Nunes , coming off the bench, managed to find the net in the 82nd minute to ignite hopes of a miracle comeback for the home supporters. As the match entered stoppage time, the atmosphere turned frantic. Following yellow cards for Joedrick Pupe and Loic Mbe Soh , the latter suffered a moment of misfortune. In the 90+3 minute, Loic Mbe Soh inadvertently turned the ball into his own net. While the late surge provided a dramatic conclusion, the early groundwork laid by Lommel United proved decisive in this pulsating encounter."
